CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ elements deduced from the pattern: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Each argument for a function parameter pack `T *...' recorded its own type
(int *) as the next element of T, so the pack was <int *, ...> and the
expanded parameters `int **' did not match.  `const T &...' lost its const
when the element replaced the pattern's decl-specifiers.
